  "body": "The maintainer asked for this work, in his own words (2026-11-19, quoted in #2818):\n\n> Issue; P4; Solidcraft has a very good viewport menu, feature we wanna copy is \"Shaded with edges, Shaded, Wireframe, Shaded with hidden edges\". The \"look at\" feature, and the graphic settings\n\nThis issue is the part of #2818 that its first PR does not include. #2818 permits the split (\"If the work is large, split it\").\n\n## State of the code\n\nThe PR of #2818 adds the Display menu to the viewport toolbar (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/display_menu.rs`). The menu has:\n\n- the four display modes;\n- \"Look at a face\" (one click on a model face or a stock face);\n- a Graphics group with \"Grid\", \"Origin axes\" and the projection.\n\n## Wanted\n\nAdd these entries to the Graphics group of the Display menu:\n\n1. A quality preset: \"Performance\" and \"Quality\". A preset sets the switches below. The menu shows which preset is active. If the user changes one switch, no preset is active.\n2. \"Ground shadow\": a soft shadow of the model on the ground grid plane.\n3. \"Ambient occlusion\": darker shading in the corners of the model.\n4. \"Look at\" for a picked plane that is not a model face: a work plane of the WCS, or a construction plane.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- Each switch is view state. It is a direct field write and is never a command. It is saved in `view.json` with the display mode (`camcraft_app::view::ViewPrefs`). An old file without the field loads the default.\n- Calculate the shadow data and the occlusion data one time for each geometry change, and cache them. Do not rebuild them on a frame. The frame target is under 10 ms. The \"Performance\" preset must keep this target on a large model. Add a counter test for each cache (`crates/ui/AGENTS.md`, \"Frame cost\").\n- Add each new pass to `crates/ui/src/draw_list.rs`, so that a test can read the draw list.\n- The wasm build uses the same settings. Hide a setting that the wasm renderer cannot draw. The menu must say nothing false.\n- Use plain English labels. Each entry has a tooltip.\n- Write the shadow pass and the occlusion pass from published graphics literature. Use no SolidCraft material (`crates/ui/AGENTS.md`, \"Icons and assets\").\n- The PR needs before and after screenshots. Tests assert labels, roles, the checked state, the state field and the draw list. They do not assert pixels. A PR never changes a snapshot PNG.\n\n## Done means\n\n- A test shows that each new entry sets its state field and that a preset sets its switches.\n- A test shows the draw list with the shadow pass and with the occlusion pass, on and off.\n- A counter test shows that a still frame builds no shadow data and no occlusion data.\n- A test shows that \"Look at\" turns the view to face a picked work plane.\n- The PR has the screenshots.\n",
